WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.793
Build a token hierarchy.

00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:05.828
A token gives a visual decision a reusable name.

00:00:05.828 --> 00:00:11.207
Separate raw values from their purpose before binding them to a component.

00:00:11.207 --> 00:00:14.345
Indigo 600 stores a single color value.

00:00:14.345 --> 00:00:17.931
Action primary describes when the color is used.

00:00:17.931 --> 00:00:20.621
Button fill references the semantic token.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:22.413
Define component states.

00:00:22.413 --> 00:00:27.397
A button needs a consistent response to pointer, keyboard, and loading events.

00:00:27.397 --> 00:00:31.550
Begin with the action that a learner wants to take.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.872
Use the primary fill for an available action.

00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:38.610
Draw a visible ring when focus reaches the button.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.518
Keep the label width and announce progress.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.734
Release a system change.

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:48.936
Test a shared component against real screens before releasing a new version.

00:00:48.936 --> 00:00:52.838
Capture what changed so other teams can adopt it.

00:00:52.838 --> 00:00:56.740
Place the old and new components side by side.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.775
Test the update with keyboard and touch.

00:00:59.775 --> 00:01:02.376
Record affected states and migration steps.

